    <GaugingStation location="Abington" name="Clyde" number="84040">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Station built to improve flood warning in the Clyde catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Station spills into right floodplain after around 2m and then into left floodplain after around 2.8m. Rating based on gaugings up to ~1.6m and thereafter higher flow estimates are informed by velocity indexing from a fixed ADCP and floodplain modelling.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station, the most upstream on the Clyde. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Two major reservoirs in the catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Heavily grazed uplands and heather moor. Large wind farms have been installed in the catchment since the station was built.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Although there are few gaugings above QMED, ratings takes into account out of bank flow." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
